<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">8 December in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 8 December, from 395 to 1991.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">395 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,631 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Northern Wei destroys the Later Yan army at Canhe Slope</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-daowu-of-northern-wei">Tuoba Gui</a>'s Northern Wei forces surprised the retreating Later Yan army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murong-bao">Murong Bao</a>, sent on a punitive campaign against its former <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a>, and destroyed it. The victory opened the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-china-plain">North China Plain</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tuoba">Tuoba</a> Gui.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-canhe-slope">Battle of Canhe Slope</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/757">757 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,269 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Du Fu returns to Chang'an with the Tang emperor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The poet Du Fu, who had escaped <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/changan">Chang'an</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/an-lushan-rebellion">An Lushan Rebellion</a> and rejoined the court, returned to the capital with the emperor after government forces recaptured it. Nearly 1,500 poems attributed to him survive.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/changan">Chang'an</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/an-lushan-rebellion">An Lushan Rebellion</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1776">1776 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">250 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Washington's army retreats across the Delaware</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The last of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-washington">George Washington</a>'s beaten Continental Army crossed the Delaware into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pennsylvania">Pennsylvania</a>, taking every boat to stop British pursuit. Weeks later he crossed back to strike at Trenton.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1777">1777 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">249 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Sir William Howe withdraws to Philadelphia after White Marsh</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The British commander-in-chief, Sir William Howe, withdrew his troops to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philadelphia">Philadelphia</a>, ending the Battle of White Marsh, a series of skirmishes around Whitemarsh Township, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pennsylvania">Pennsylvania</a>. It was the last major engagement of 1777 between British and American forces.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-revolutionary-war">American Revolutionary War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1854">1854 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">172 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pius IX defines the Immaculate Conception</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In the bull Ineffabilis Deus, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-pius-ix">Pope Pius IX</a> declared as dogma that the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mary-mother-of-jesus">Virgin Mary</a> was conceived without original sin. Other Christian traditions do not accept the doctrine.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1941">1941 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">85 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The United States and Britain declare war on Japan</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Franklin Roosevelt asked Congress to declare war, calling 7 December 'a date which will live in infamy'. Congress agreed within the hour, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> also declared war on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1980">1980 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">46 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">John Lennon is shot dead in New York</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Mark <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a> Chapman shot John Lennon outside the Dakota building in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manhattan">Manhattan</a>. The killing of the former Beatle prompted vigils around the world.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1991">1991 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">35 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Leaders of Russia, Ukraine and Belarus agree to dissolve the USSR</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Meeting in the Belovezha Forest, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boris-yeltsin">Boris Yeltsin</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leonid-kravchuk">Leonid Kravchuk</a> and Stanislav Shushkevich declared that the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> had ceased to exist and created the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/commonwealth-of-independent-states">Commonwealth of Independent States</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a></div></div></li></ol>
