<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 8 December <span class="n">7</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/arnulf-of-carinthia"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/arnulf-of-carinthia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Arnulf of Carinthia</span><span class="tp">c. 850–899</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/berthold-iv-of-zahringen"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/berthold-iv-of-zahringen.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Berthold IV of Zähringen</span><span class="tp">c. 1125–1186</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/nicholas-ii-of-opava"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/nicholas-ii-of-opava.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Nicholas II of Opava</span><span class="tp">c. 1288–1365</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ivan-gundulic"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ivan-gundulic.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ivan Gundulić</span><span class="tp">1589–1638</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/john-pym"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/john-pym.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">John Pym</span><span class="tp">1584–1643</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/elizabeth-charlotte-madame-palatine"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/elizabeth-charlotte-madame-palatine.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Elizabeth Charlotte, Madame Palatine</span><span class="tp">1652–1722</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/keith-holyoake"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/keith-holyoake.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Keith Holyoake</span><span class="tp">1904–1983</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
